 //All texts are presented AS IS and the provider of this library is not liable for any consequences resulting from using it in any way. Unless specified otherwise, the following texts for each component are public domain.

// The following relay models have a spice model, which is idealized. Please be aware of the fact that the real model 
// might work in similar way as the idealized ones in some circuits, but also will work differently in other circuits.
//For example:
// - These models have an idealized rise and fall time, which means that the switch time between high and low voltage here is only the time step of the simulation. Real components often have a larger switch time. Relays typically a few milliseconds, in some circuits this might be relevant.
// - Many real relays have a mechanical vibration after switching, in the so-called "bounce-time" so that the connection in the switch vibrates too. This vibration is not modeled here.
// - Real relays need a few milliseconds to switch, in the so called "switch-time" before it starts bouncing. This is not modeled here
// -> So for the users: Please be aware that there are the differences between the real components and the idealized model
// -> So for the jurists: this library is presented AS IS. We are not liable of any consequences resulting from it in any way.
// -> So for the helping hands: there is still a lot TODO in this library to make more realistic models:
//      Someone who has a more realistic model which also works reliably in ngspice is very welcome to add it to the library
//      also you may of course contact us.
//    Also this library only contains the relays alphabetically from A like "American Zettler" to F like "FINDER". Further relays: TODO


// ---- Part 1 - Relays ----
<Component>
    <Description>
        A relay.
		You can either define its parameters, or you can select a model.
				
		---- A: parameters  IF [modeltype]THEN(please select the parameter list instead of a model to see the parameter description) ----

		ELSE ---- 
		you can define a relay by giving its parameters:
		
		A bistable (latching) relay or monostable relay,or AC-relay, depending on parameter:
        -If the parameter ampere_off is equal to Pc*ampere_on, with Pc a positive constant, typically between 0.05 and 0.35,
        then it is a monostable relay: The relay is reset at a current lower than the set-on-current, because the iron core 
        of the coil is still magnetized. Therefor a lower current keeps the relay on.
        -If the parameter ampere_off is equal to Nc*ampere_on, with Nc a negative constant, typically between 0 and -1,
        then it is a bistable relay
        
        This model contains fuses to simulate the fact that the coil and the connections of the switches can get destroyed by exceeding the maximal ratings.
        The coil or switch is considered "destroyed" as soon current of ampere_destroy_coil or ampere_destroy_switch is reached, see Spice section below.

		
		--necessary parameters:--
		volt_n is the nominal voltage. (May only be omitted, when volt_set and volt_reset are both given.)

        --optional parameters:--
		volt_set is the voltage at which the coil gets activated (green). When not given, then automatically set to 0.8x volt_n.
		volt_reset is the voltage at which the coil gets deactivated (red). When not given, then automatically set to 0.6x volt_n.
		ohm_coil is the resistance of the coil in Ohms. When not given then 100 Ohms.
		nr_switches is the number of switches. May be 1 or 2. If not given or any other number given then set to 1.		
        switch_type is the type of the switch(es). May be NO=nomally open (default), NC=nomally contacted or CO=Changeover.
        henry_coil is the inductance of the coil. When not given, then so small that it is irrelevant (1pH).
        coil_direction is the direction of the coil: 
         -> TopNeg_PosBottom and BottomNeg_PosTop are for directed coils,
         -> AC is for alternating currents,
         -> and if that variable does not exist, then the direction of the current is irrelevant,so the coil works in both directions.
        f_n is the nominal frequency for AC coils. (when f_n exists, but coil_direction is not AC, then f_n is ignored.)
            ->  when not given, then default frequency is 50Hertz for AC coils.
        volt_destroy_coil is the voltage at which the coil burns through.
            -> When not given, then so large, that it's irrelevant (1MegaVolt)
        amp_destroy_switch is the current at which the contacted switch burns through.
             -> When not given, then so large, that it's irrelevant (equivalent of 1MegaVolt/internal resistance)
		ENDIF
		---- B:  model IF![modeltype]THEN(please select one of the available types to see their description) ENDIF---- 
		IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH DIP THEN -- DIPxx series: ----
			model= DIPnn-qFmm-ppO
			
			where:
			nn is the nominal voltage in two digits: 05 12 15 or 24
			q is the number of switches: 1 or 2
			F is the contact form in one letter: A B or C (A=normally Open , B=Normally Closed , C=Changeover)
			mm is the switch model in two digits: 72 75 or 90
			pp is the pin out in two digits: 10 11 12 13 19 21 or 51
			O at the end is the option, and is optional. can be A B C L D E F , but is ignored
			
			For example, DIP05-1A72-10 is a valid value.
			See datasheet at https:standexelectronics.com/wp-content/uploads/datasheet_reed_relay_DIP.pdf
			ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH AZ850 THEN
			-- AZ850 series --- 
			model=AZ850-x or AZ850P1-x

			where:
			AZ850- are the single side stable relays,
			AZ850P1- are the bistable (latching ) relays, and
			x is the nominal VDC voltage, one of the values: 3 5 6 9 12 24

			For example, model=AZ850-5 describes a normal 5 Volt relay, 
			and model=AZ850P1-24 describes a latching 24 Volt relay. 
		ENDIF
		IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-30.22 THEN -- Finder 30.22 series --
			model=FINDER-30.22.7.vvv
			where vvv is the three digit voltage: 005 006 009 012 024 or 048
			
			For example, model=FINDER-30.22.7.012 describes a 12 Volt relay. 
			
			The Finder 30.22 series is a relay with two Changeover ("CO") switches.
			See datasheet at www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-30.pdf
			ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-32.21 THEN
			-- Finder 32.21 series --
			model=FINDER-32.21.7.vvv and 
			model=FINDER-32.21.7.vvv.x300
			where vvv is the three digit voltage: 005 006 009 012 024 or 048
			
			Without the optional ending ".x300"  this relay has changeover (CO) contacts, with that ending the contacts are normally open(NO).
		ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-34.51 THEN -- Finder 34.51 series --
			model=FINDER-34.51.7.vvv and
			model=FINDER-34.51.7.vvv.x300
			where vvv is the three digit voltage: 005 012 024 048 or 060 
			
			The Finder 34.51 is a relay with one switch. That switch is normally open(NO) when the optional ending ".x300" is given, and changeover(CO) otherwise.
			That switch has a maximal current of 6 A.
			See datasheet www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-34.pdf
		ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-36.11 THEN-- Finder 36.11 series --
			model=FINDER-36.11.9.vvv
			IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN
				wobei vvv die Spannung mit drei Ziffern ist: 003 005 006 009 012 024 oder 048 *
				
				Das Finder 36.11 ist ein Relais mit einem Schalter. Dieser Schalter ist immer ein Wechsler. Es hat einen maximalen Dauerstrom von 10 A, 
				und einen Spitzenstrom von 15 A.
				
				Mehr Details siehe Datenblatt unter www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-36.pdf
				
				Zum Beispiel beschreibt model=FINDER-36.11.9.012 das 12-Volt-Relais.
				
				* (im Gegensatz zu den anderen Serien kann die Simulation der FINDER-36.11.9.vvv auch mit anderen vvv Werten im Bereich 001 bis 999 laufen.
					Trotzdem gibt es die realen Relais nur mit den aufgelisteten Werten. Daher wird empfohlen, einen dieser Werte zu nehmen.) 
			ELSE
				where vvv is the three digit voltage: 003 005 006 009 012 024 or 048 *
				
				The Finder 36.11 is a relay with one switch. That switch is always a changeover (CO). It has a maximal permanent current of 10 Ampere.
				More details see at datasheet www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-36.pdf
				
				For example, model=FINDER-36.11.9.012 describes the 12-Volt-relais.
				
				* (unlike most other series, the simulation of the FINDER-36.11.9.vvv can also run with other vvv values in range from 001 to 999.
					Nevertheless the real components of that series are only the ones listed above. Therefor using one of these is recommended.)
			ENDIF
		ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-40. THEN-- Finder 40 series --
			model=FINDER-40.hh.c.vvv   where
			 hh is a two-digit code for the housing (not relevant for the simulation). One of the values 11 12 31 32 51 52 61 or 62
			 c is the coil form, 7 for sensitive DC coil, 8 for AC coil, 9 for normal DC coil
			 vvv is the three digit voltage: 005 006 009 012 014 018 021 024 028 036 048 060 090 110 120 125 230 or 240
			 
			For example FINDER-40.31.8.230 describes an AC relay for the standard 230V-50Hz input.

			* (unlike most other series, the simulation of the FINDER-40 series can also run with other vvv values in range from 001 to 999.
				Nevertheless the real components of that series are only the ones listed above. Therefor using one of these is recommended.)
		ENDIF IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-41.52 THEN-- Finder 41.52 series --
			model=FINDER-41.52.c.vvv where
			c is the coil form, 8 for AC or 9 for DC (form 6 for bistable coil is not available in this model)
			vvv is the three digit voltage. 
			For AC coil either 024 or 230, for DC coil one of the following 005 006 012 024 048 060 or 110
		ENDIF
    </Description>
	<Default_Values>
		volt_n=5.0V // a simple relais model with nominal voltage of 5 Volt
		volt_n=24V switch_type=CO // relais model with changeover contact (CO=changeover, NO=normally open, NC=normally closed)
		ohm_coil=150 volt_set=4V volt_reset=3V nr_switches=1 switch_type=NO // relay defined by some parameters.
		ohm_coil=150 volt_set=4V volt_reset=3V nr_switches=1 switch_type=NO henry_coil=22m coil_direction=AC f_n=50Hz volt_destroy_coil=9V amp_destroy_switch=4.2A // relay defined by all parameters 
		volt_set=4V volt_reset=-4V coil_direction=BottomNeg_PosTop // a bistable relay, by setting the reset voltage to a negative value and defining the polarity of the coil.
		model=DIP05-1A72-10 // A relay of the DIPxx series with 5 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch, A=NO contacts.
		model=DIP12-2B72-10 // A relay of the DIPxx series with 12 Volt nominal voltage, 2 switches, B=NC contacts.
		model=DIP24-1C72-10 // A relay of the DIPxx series with 24 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch, C=CO contacts
		model=AZ850-5 // A relay of the AZ850 series with 5 Volt nominal voltage
		model=AZ850P1-5 // A relay of the AZ850 series with 5 Volt nominal voltage and a latching coil.
		model=FINDER-30.22.7.012 // A relay of the Finder Serie 30.22 with 12 Volt nominal voltage, 2 switches, CO contacts.
		model=FINDER-32.21.7.024 // A relay of the Finder Serie 32.21 with 24 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch, and CO=changeover contacts.
		model=FINDER-32.21.7.024.x300 // A relay of the Finder Serie 32.21 with 24 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch, and NO=normally open contacts.
		model=FINDER-34.51.7.005 // A relay of the Finder Serie 34.51 with 5 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch, and CO=changeover contacts.
		model=FINDER-34.51.7.005.x300 // A relay of the Finder Serie 34.51 with 5 Volt nominal voltage, 1 switch and NO=nomally open contacts.
		model=FINDER-36.11.9.012 // A relay of the Finder Serie 36.11 with 12 Volt nominal voltage 1 Switch and CO=changeover contacts
		model=FINDER-40.11.7.018 // A relay of the Finder Serie 40 with 18 Volt nominal voltage and sensitive DC coil
		model=FINDER-40.11.8.018 // A relay of the Finder Serie 40 with 18 Volt nominal voltage and AC coil
		model=FINDER-40.11.9.018 // A relay of the Finder Serie 40 with 18 Volt nominal voltage and normal DC coil
		model=FINDER-41.52.9.024 // A relay of the Finder Serie 41.52 with 24 Volt nominal voltage and DC coil
		model=FINDER-41.52.8.230 // A relay of the Finder Serie 41.52 with 230 Volt nominal voltage and AC coil - for the standard-230V-50Hz power supply.
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L anicad:Relay
	</eeschema_sch>
   <eeschema_symbol>
   		//preparation - collect modeltype:
		DEFINE [modeltype] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:model IN:[value]
		IF [modeltype] THEN
			
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH DIP THEN
				INCLUDE standex_dip
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH AZ850 THEN
				INCLUDE AZ850
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-30.22 THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_30_22
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-32.21 THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_32_21
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-34.51 THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_34_51
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-36.11 THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_36_11
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-40. THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_40
			ENDIF
			IF [modeltype] STARTS_WITH FINDER-41.52 THEN
				INCLUDE FINDER_41_52
			ENDIF
		ELSE // no relay model type given: search parameters directly
			DEFINE [volt_n] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_n IN:[value]
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:ohm_coil IN:[value]
			DEFINE [volt_set] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_set IN:[value]
			DEFINE [volt_reset] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_reset IN:[value]
			DEFINE [nr_switches] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:nr_switches IN:[value]
			DEFINE [switch_type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:switch_type IN:[value] 
			DEFINE [henry_coil] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:henry_coil IN:[value]
			DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:coil_direction IN:[value]
			DEFINE [f_n] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:f_n IN:[value] 
		ENDIF
		
		// preparation - collect parameters:
		IF ![volt_n] THEN DEFINE [volt_n] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_n IN:[value] ENDIF
		DEFINE [volt_n] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_n]
		
		IF ![ohm_coil] THEN DEFINE [ohm_coil] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:ohm_coil IN:[value] ENDIF
		DEFINE [ohm_coil] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm_coil]
		IF ![ohm_coil] THEN DEFINE [ohm_coil] 100 ENDIF
		
		IF ![volt_set] THEN DEFINE [volt_set] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_set IN:[value] ENDIF
		DEFINE [volt_set] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_set]
		IF ![volt_set] THEN DEFINE [volt_set] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[volt_n] AND:0.8 ENDIF // Default set voltage = 0,8 x nominal voltage
		IF ![volt_set] THEN DEFINE [volt_set] 0.8 ENDIF // Default value 0,8 Volt (When nominal voltage also not given)
		
		IF ![volt_reset] THEN DEFINE [volt_reset] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_reset IN:[value] ENDIF
		DEFINE [volt_reset] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_reset]	
		IF ![volt_reset] THEN DEFINE [volt_reset] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[volt_n] AND:0.6 ENDIF // Default reset voltage = 0,6 x nominal voltage
		IF ![volt_reset] THEN DEFINE [volt_reset] 0.6 ENDIF // Default value 0,6 Volt (When nominal voltage also not given)
		
		IF ![nr_switches] THEN DEFINE [nr_switches] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:nr_switches IN:[value] ENDIF
		IF ![nr_switches] || [nr_switches] HIGHER_THAN 2 || [nr_switches] LOWER_THAN 1 THEN DEFINE [nr_switches] 1 ENDIF
		
		// switch type may be NO or NC or CO. Otherwise set to default value NO=normally open.
		IF ![switch_type] THEN DEFINE [switch_type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:switch_type IN:[value] ENDIF
		IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THENELSE DEFINE [switch_type] NO ENDIF 
	
		IF ![henry_coil] THEN DEFINE [henry_coil] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:henry_coil IN:[value] ENDIF
		DEFINE [henry_coil] AS_NUMBER OF:[henry_coil]
		
		// coil_direction may be Null or have the values TopNeg_PosBottom or BottomNeg_PosTop or AC
		IF ![coil_direction] THEN DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:coil_direction IN:[value] ENDIF
		IF [coil_direction] EQUAL_TO TopNeg_PosBottom || [coil_direction] EQUAL_TO BottomNeg_PosTop || [coil_direction] EQUAL_TO AC 
		THENELSE DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_NULL ENDIF
		
		IF ![f_n] THEN DEFINE [f_n] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:f_n IN:[value] ENDIF
		IF ![f_n] THEN DEFINE [f_n] 50 ENDIF // ac coils have a default frequency of fifty Hertz.
		
    DRAW 
       IF[nr_switches]EQUAL_TO1THEN//relay with one switch
        IF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN
            S -400 200 400 -200 0 1 10 f
        ELSE
            IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN
                S -400 200 350 -200 0 1 10 f
            ELSE
                <Dialog type="error">types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>//TODO make message more specific!
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
        S -325 75 -75 -75 0 1 10 N
        P 2 0 1 10 -300 -75 -100 75 N
        P 2 0 1 0 -200 -200 -200 -75 N
        P 2 0 1 0 -200 200 -200 75 N
        P 2 0 1 10 -75 0 -50 0 N
        P 2 0 1 10 -25 0 0 0 N
        P 2 0 1 10 25 0 50 0 N
        P 2 0 1 10 25 0 50 0 N
        P 2 0 1 10 75 0 100 0 N
        P 2 0 1 10 125 0 150 0 N
        P 2 0 1 0 200 -100 200 -200 N
        //coil pins:
        IF[coil_direction]THEN
            IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS TopNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosBottom THEN
                X coil_pos 2 -200 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                X coil_neg 6 -200 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                P 2 0 1 0 -240 -250 -220 -250 N
                P 2 0 1 0 -230 -260 -230 -240 N
                P 2 0 1 0 -240 250 -220 250 N
            ELSE IF[coil_direction]CONTAINS BottomNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosTop THEN
                X coil_neg 2 -200 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                X coil_pos 6 -200 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                P 2 0 1 0 -240 250 -220 250 N
                P 2 0 1 0 -230 260 -230 240 N
                P 2 0 1 0 -240 -250 -220 -250 N
            ELSE IF[coil_direction] EQUAL_TO AC THEN
                X coil_neg 2 -200 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                X coil_pos 6 -200 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                 A -240 250 30 0 1800    0 0 0 0 -220 250 -220 250
                A -290 250 30 1800 3600 0 0 0 0 -270 250 -210 250
                A -240 -250 30 1800 3600 0 0 0 0 -220 -250 -220 -250
                A -290 -250 30 0 1800    0 0 0 0 -210 -250 -210 -250
            ELSE <Dialog type="error">the coil direction value, [coil_direction], is not a valid one for relay model [model]
            name [name] ,value [value] at ([xpos]|[ypos])</Dialog>
            ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
        ELSE // no directed coils (still have coil_pos and coil_neg, but the direction of current is no more important)
            X coil_pos 2 -200 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
            X coil_neg 6 -200 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
        ENDIF
        // 1 switch
        X sw1_from 1 200 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
        IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN
            X sw1_toA 7 300 300 200 D 0 50 1 1 P
            //P 4 0 0 0 200 150 200 100 175 125 200 150 N
            P 2 0 1 20 200 -100 125 150 N
            //P 2 0 0 0 200 150 200 200 N //connection line (single)
        ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NC THEN
            X sw1_toB 7 200 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            P 4 0 0 0 200 150 200 100 175 125 200 150 F
            P 2 0 1 20 200 -100 175 150 N
             P 2 0 0 0 200 150 200 200 N //connection line (single)
        ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN
            X sw1_toB 1 100 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw1_toA 14 300 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            P 4 0 0 0 300 150 300 100 275 125 300 150 N
            P 3 0 1 0 100 100 125 125 100 150 F
            P 2 0 1 20 200 -100 125 150 N
            P 2 0 0 0 100 150 100 200 N //connection line (left)
            P 2 0 0 0 300 150 300 200 N //connection line (right)
        ELSE<Dialog type="error">drawing for types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>//TODO make message more specific!
        ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
    
      ELSEIF[nr_switches]EQUAL_TO2THEN
        IF[switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN
            S -600 200 600 -200 0 1 10 f
            S -525 75 -275 -75 0 1 10 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -500 -75 -300 75 N
            P 2 0 1 0 -400 -200 -400 -75 N
            P 2 0 1 0 -400 200 -400 75 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -275 0 -250 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -225 0 -200 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -175 0 -150 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -125 0 -100 0 N
            P 2 0 1 0 -100 100 -100 200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -75 0 -50 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -25 0 0 0 N
            P 2 0 1 20 0 -100 -75 150 N
            P 2 0 1 0 0 -100 0 -200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 25 0 50 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 75 0 100 0 N
            P 2 0 1 0 100 100 100 200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 125 0 150 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 175 0 200 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 225 0 250 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 275 0 300 0 N
            P 2 0 1 0 300 100 300 200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 325 0 350 0 N
            P 2 0 1 20 400 -100 325 150 N
            P 2 0 1 0 400 -100 400 -200 N
            P 2 0 1 0 500 100 500 200 N
            P 3 0 1 0 -100 100 -75 125 -100 150 F
            P 3 0 1 0 100 100 75 125 100 150 N
            P 3 0 1 0 300 100 325 125 300 150 F
            P 3 0 1 0 500 100 475 125 500 150 N
            IF[coil_direction]THEN
                IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS TopNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosBottom THEN
                    X coil_pos 2 -400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                    X coil_neg 6 -400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                    P 2 0 1 0 -440 -250 -420 -250 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -430 -260 -430 -240 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -440 250 -420 250 N
                ELSE IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS BottomNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosTop THEN
                    X coil_neg 2 -400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                    X coil_pos 6 -400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                    P 2 0 1 0 -440 250 -420 250 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -430 260 -430 240 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -440 -250 -420 -250 N
                ELSE IF[coil_direction] EQUAL_TO AC THEN
                    X coil_neg 2 -400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                    X coil_pos 6 -400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                    A -440 250 30 0 1800    0 0 0 0 -420 250 -420 250
                    A -490 250 30 1800 3600 0 0 0 0 -470 250 -410 250
                    A -440 -250 30 1800 3600 0 0 0 0 -420 -250 -420 -250
                    A -490 -250 30 0 1800    0 0 0 0 -470 -250 -410 -250
                ELSE 
                    <Dialog type="error">the coil direction value, [coil_direction], is not a valid one for relay model [model]                name [name] ,value [value] at ([xpos]|[ypos])</Dialog>
                ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
            ELSE // no directed coils (still have coil_pos and coil_neg, but the direction of current is no more important)
                X coil_pos 4 -400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                X coil_neg 5 -400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            ENDIF
            X sw1_from 1    0 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw2_from 14 400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw1_toB 7 -100 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw1_toA 6 100 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw2_toB 8 300 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw2_toA 9 500 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
        ELSE // switch_type NC or NO
            S -500 200 450 -200 0 1 10 f
            P 2 0 1 0 -300 -200 -300 -75 N
            P 2 0 1 0 -300 200 -300 75 N
            S -425 75 -175 -75 0 1 10 N
            P 2 0 0 0 100 150 100 200 N
            P 2 0 0 0 400 150 400 200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -400 -75 -200 75 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -175 0 -150 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -125 0 -100 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -75 0 -50 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -75 0 -50 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 -25 0 0 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 25 0 50 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 75 0 100 0 N
            P 2 0 1 0 100 -100 100 -200 N
            P 2 0 1 10 125 0 150 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 175 0 200 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 225 0 250 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 275 0 300 0 N
            P 2 0 1 10 325 0 350 0 N
            P 2 0 1 0 400 -100 400 -200 N
            IF[coil_direction]THEN
                IF[coil_direction]CONTAINS TopNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosBottom THEN
                    X coil_pos 2 -300 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                    X coil_neg 6 -300 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                    P 2 0 1 0 -340 -250 -320 -250 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -330 -260 -330 -240 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -340 250 -320 250 N
                ELSE IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS BottomNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosTop THEN
                    X coil_neg 2 -300 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                    X coil_pos 6 -300 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                    P 2 0 1 0 -340 250 -320 250 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -330 260 -330 240 N
                    P 2 0 1 0 -340 -250 -320 -250 N
                ELSE 
                    <Dialog type="error">the coil direction value, [coil_direction], is not a valid one for relay model [model]                name [name] ,value [value] at ([xpos]|[ypos])</Dialog>
                ENDIF ENDIF
            ELSE // no directed coils (still have coil_pos and coil_neg, but the direction of current is no more important)
                X coil_pos 4 -400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
                X coil_neg 5 -400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
            ENDIF            
            X sw1_from 1 100 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
            X sw2_from 14 400 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 P
            IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN
                X sw1_toA 7 100 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                X sw2_toA 8 400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                P 4 0 0 0 100 150 100 100 75 125 100 150 N
                P 4 0 0 0 400 150 400 100 375 125 400 150 N
                P 2 0 1 20 400 -100 325 150 N
                P 2 0 1 20 100 -100 25 150 N
            ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NC THEN
                X sw1_toB 7 100 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                X sw2_toB 8 400 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 P
                P 4 0 0 0 100 150 100 100 75 125 100 150 F
                P 4 0 0 0 400 150 400 100 375 125 400 150 F
                P 2 0 1 20 400 -100 375 150 N
                P 2 0 1 20 100 -100 75 150 N
            ENDIF ENDIF 
        ENDIF
        ELSE<Dialog type="error">Relay type [model] named [name] at ([xpos]|[ypos]) has [nr_switches] switches, but the symbol 
            drawing for relays only is specified for 1 or 2 switches.</Dialog>
      ENDIF ENDIF //[nr_switches]
    ENDDRAW
    </eeschema_symbol>
	<animation>
		// calculate voltage of the coil:
		IF [coil_direction] THEN
			 IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS BottomNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosTop THEN
				DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[coil_pos] AND:V[coil_neg]
			ENDIF
			IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS TopNeg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS PosBottom THEN
				DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[coil_pos] AND:V[coil_neg]
			ENDIF
			IF[coil_direction] EQUAL_TO AC THEN
				DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[coil_pos] AND:V[coil_neg]
				DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[v_coil]
			ENDIF
		ELSE
			DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[coil_pos] AND:V[coil_neg]
			DEFINE [v_coil] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[v_coil]
		ENDIF
		
		// set the color of the coil:
		IF      [v_coil] EQUAL_OR_HIGHER_THAN [volt_set] THEN DEFINE [coil_color] #00FF00 // green coil for on.
		ELSE IF [v_coil] LOWER_THAN         [volt_reset] THEN DEFINE [coil_color] #FF0000 // red coil for off.
		ELSE 	DEFINE [coil_color] #888800 // yellow coil for intermediary coil state keeping the switch as it is.
			 ENDIF
		ENDIF		 
		
		// calculate the resistanc(es) of the 1st switch(es)
		IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN
			DEFINE [v_to1a] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[sw1_toA] AND:V[sw1_from]
			DEFINE [i_to1a] I[sw1_toA]
			DEFINE [r_to1a] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[v_to1a] AND:[i_to1a]
			DEFINE [r_to1a] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[r_to1a]
			IF !IS_NUMBER [r_to1a] THEN DEFINE [r_to1a] -1 ENDIF
			IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						DEFINE [switch_color_a] #880000 // red for off
			    ELSE    DEFINE [switch_color_a] #008800 // green for on.
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC THEN
			DEFINE [v_to1b] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[sw1_toB] AND:V[sw1_from]
			DEFINE [i_to1b] I[sw1_toB]
			DEFINE [r_to1b] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[v_to1b] AND:[i_to1b]
			DEFINE [r_to1b] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[r_to1b]
			IF !IS_NUMBER [r_to1b] THEN DEFINE [r_to1b] -1 ENDIF
			IF [r_to1b] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN 
					DEFINE [switch_color_b] #880000 // red for off
			ELSE 	DEFINE [switch_color_b] #008800 // green for on.
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		
		IF [nr_switches] EQUAL_TO1THEN // draw 1 switch:
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN
				IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 80 -155 240 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area
					IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line  200 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ELSE
						<Line  200 100 100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
				<Polygon_4 300 -150 300 -100 275 -125 300 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>//triangle indicating NO type
			ENDIF
			
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC THEN
				IF [r_to1b] HIGHER THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 80 -155 240 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area
				
					IF  [r_to1b] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line  200 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ELSE
						<Line  200 100 -25 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
				<Polygon_4 200 -150 200 -100 175 -125 200 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1>//triangle indicating NC type
			ENDIF
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN
				IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 200 -155 120 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area for switch A
					IF [r_to1a] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line 200 100 100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ELSE
					<Rectangle 200 -155 120 255 #444444 2 1 #444444 1 0.9> // gray switch area for switch A	
				ENDIF
				IF [r_to1b] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 80 -155 120 255 [switch_color_b] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area for switch B
					IF [r_to1b] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
					    <Line 200 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ELSE
					<Rectangle 80 -155 120 255 #444444 2 1 #444444 1 0.9> // gray switch area for switch B
					
				ENDIF
				//P 3 0 1 0 100 100 125 125 100 150 F
				<Polygon_3 100 -100 125 -125 100 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1> // filled triangle for switch B, normally closed
				//P 4 0 0 0 300 150 300 100 275 125 300 150 N
				<Polygon_4 300 -150 300 -100 275 -125 300 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>// non-filled triangle for switch A, normally open
			ENDIF
		ELSE // draw 2 switches:
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN
				IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 0 -155 400 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area
					IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line  100 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1> // 1st switch
						<Line  400 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1> // 2nd switch (also controlled by 1st switch, because running the same way.)
					ELSE
						<Line  100 100 -25 -255 #000088 2 1> 
						<Line  400 100 -25 -255 #000088 2 1> 
					ENDIF
				<Polygon_4 100 -150 100 -100  75 -125 100 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>// non-filled triangle indicating NO type
				<Polygon_4 400 -150 400 -100 375 -125 400 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>// non-filled triangle indicating NO type
				ENDIF
			ENDIF
			
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC THEN
				IF [r_to1b] HIGHER THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 0 -155 400 255 [switch_color_b] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area
					IF  [r_to1b] HIGHER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line  100 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1> // 1st switch
						<Line  400 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1> // 2nd switch
					ELSE
						<Line  100 100 -25 -255 #000088 2 1> 
						<Line  400 100 -25 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
				<Polygon_4 100 -150 100 -100  75 -125 100 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1>// filled triangle indicating NC type
				<Polygon_4 400 -150 400 -100 375 -125 400 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1>// filled triangle indicating NC type
			ENDIF
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN
				IF [r_to1a] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle 00 -155 120 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> 
					<Rectangle 400 -155 120 255 [switch_color_a] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> 
					
					IF [r_to1a] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
						<Line  0 100 100 -255 #000088 2 1>
						<Line  400 100 100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
				IF [r_to1b] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					<Rectangle -120 -155 120 255 [switch_color_b] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area for switch B
					<Rectangle 280 -155 120 255 [switch_color_b] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.9> // colored switch area for switch B
					
					IF [r_to1b] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN [ohm_thresh] THEN
					    <Line  0 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1>
						<Line  400 100 -100 -255 #000088 2 1>
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
				<Polygon_3 -100 -100 -75 -125 -100 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1> 
				<Polygon_3 300 -100 325 -125 300 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 1> 
				
				<Polygon_4 100 -150 100 -100  75 -125  100 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>
				<Polygon_4 500 -150 500 -100  475 -125 500 -150 #000088 2 1 #000080 2 0>
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		
		// draw the coil for 1 switch:
		IF[nr_switches] EQUAL_TO1THEN
			<Rectangle -325 -75 250 150 [coil_color] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.5> // animate the coil
		ELSE 
		// draw the coil for 2 switches:
			IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN
				<Rectangle -525 -75 250 150 [coil_color] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.5> 
			ELSE
				<Rectangle -425 -75 250 150 [coil_color] 2 1 #00CCCC 1 0.5> 
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		
		
	</animation>
    <purchase>
		<link>
		<url>cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Frelais-17391.html</url>
		<title>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Uebersicht Relais ELSE Overview relaysENDIF</title>
		<detail>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Auswahl an Relais bei Conrad Electronic. Darunter eine Beschreibung. ELSE A collection of relays of various types at conrad electronic.ENDIF</detail>
		</link>
		IF [conrad_de] THEN
		<link>
		    <url>cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fp%2F[conrad_de]</url>
			<title>component of [modeltype] series</title>
			<detail>a relais of the [modeltype] series at conrad electronic. Please make sure that you select a matching relais, e.g. make sure that the nominal voltage is correct for your purpose.</detail>
		</link>
		ENDIF
	</purchase>
    <Spice>   
        //---- Pre-compiler ----
        IF ![volt_destroy_coil]   THEN DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil]   1E9 ENDIF
        IF ![volt_destroy_switch] THEN DEFINE [volt_destroy_switch] 1E9 ENDIF
        IF ![ohm_contact]         THEN DEFINE [ohm_contact]         10m ENDIF
		DEFINE [ohm_contact] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm_contact]
		IF ![ohm_isolate]         THEN DEFINE [ohm_isolate]         1E6 ENDIF
		DEFINE [ohm_isolate] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm_isolate]
		DEFINE [ohm_thresh] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[ohm_contact] AND:[ohm_isolate]
		DEFINE [ohm_thresh] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[ohm_thresh] AND:2 // threshold for animation purposes
        // ---- model ----
        .subckt relay_[individual] coil_pos coil_neg sw1_from IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN sw1_toA  ELSEIF [switch_type]EQUAL_TONCTHEN sw1_toB ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN sw1_toA sw1_toB ELSE <Dialog type="error">types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog> ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN1THEN sw2_from IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN sw2_toA  ELSEIF [switch_type]EQUAL_TONCTHEN sw2_toB ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN sw2_toA sw2_toB ELSE <Dialog type="error">types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog> ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
       //model parameters:
       .param ampere_on=[volt_set]/[ohm_coil]
       .param ampere_off=[volt_reset]/[ohm_coil]
       .param ampere_destroy_coil=[volt_destroy_coil]/[ohm_coil]
       IF[amp_destroy_switch]THEN
           .param ampere_destroy_switch=[amp_destroy_switch]
       ELSE
           .param ampere_destroy_switch=[volt_destroy_switch]/ohm_contact
        ENDIF
        IF[ohm_coil]THEN
            .param ohm_coil=[ohm_coil]
        ELSE
            <Dialog type="error">The coil resistance, [ohm_coil] is not defined for component:
                    named [name]
                    value [value]
                    model [model]
                    at ([xpos]|[ypos])
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
       IF [coil_direction]EQUAL_TO AC THEN
            IF [f_n] THEN
                .param tau_n=1/[f_n]
            ELSE
                .param tau_n=1/50
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
       IF[henry_coil]THEN
            .param henry_coil=[henry_coil]
       ELSE
            .param henry_coil=1p   //not specified in the datasheet. 
       ENDIF
       .param ohm_contact=[ohm_contact]/2 //divided by two because used in fuse and in switch.
	   
        //coil:
        l_coil coil_pos coil_lf henry_coil
        //fuse in coil (contains [ohm_coil]):
        s_fuse_coil coil_lf coil_neg broken_fuse_coil 0 fuse_coil
        //fuses in switches:
        IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN s_fuse_sw1A sw1_midA sw1_toA broken_fuse_sw1A 0 fuse_switch ELSE
        IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC THEN s_fuse_sw1B sw1_midB sw1_toB broken_fuse_sw1B 0 fuse_switch ELSE
        IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN s_fuse_sw1A sw1_midA sw1_toA broken_fuse_sw1A 0 fuse_switch
                                          s_fuse_sw1B sw1_midB sw1_toB broken_fuse_sw1B 0 fuse_switch
        ELSE <Dialog type="error"> types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>//TODO make message more specific!
        ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF 
        IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN1THEN
            IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NO THEN s_fuse_sw2A sw2_midA sw2_toA broken_fuse_sw2A 0 fuse_switch ELSE
            IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO NC THEN s_fuse_sw2B sw2_midB sw2_toB broken_fuse_sw2B 0 fuse_switch ELSE
            IF [switch_type] EQUAL_TO CO THEN s_fuse_sw2A sw2_midA sw2_toA broken_fuse_sw2A 0 fuse_switch
                                              s_fuse_sw2B sw2_midB sw2_toB broken_fuse_sw2B 0 fuse_switch
            ELSE <Dialog type="error"> types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined<Dialog type="error">//TODO make message more specific!
            ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF 
        ENDIF
        //TODO: these fuse models interrupt without any time delay. It would be more realistic to interrupt after a few ms.
        //set and hold fuses:            |<------------ set --------------->| || |<------- hold -------->|
        B_fuse_coil broken_fuse_coil 0 V=abs(I(l_coil)) > ampere_destroy_coil || V(broken_fuse_coil) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0
        B_fuse_sw1A broken_fuse_sw1A 0 V=abs(I(s1a)) > ampere_destroy_switch  || V(broken_fuse_sw1A) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0
        B_fuse_sw1B broken_fuse_sw1B 0 V=abs(I(s1b)) > ampere_destroy_switch  || V(broken_fuse_sw1B) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0
        IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN1THEN
            //set and hold fuses:            |<------------ set --------------->| || |<------- hold -------->|
            B_fuse_sw2A broken_fuse_sw2A 0 V=abs(I(s2a)) > ampere_destroy_switch  || V(broken_fuse_sw2A) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0
            B_fuse_sw2B broken_fuse_sw2B 0 V=abs(I(s2b)) > ampere_destroy_switch  || V(broken_fuse_sw2B) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0
            IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN2THEN
                <Dialog type="error">Relay type [modeltype] named [name] at ([xpos]|[ypos]) has [nr_switches] switches, but the simulation for relays only is specified for up to 2 switches.
                </Dialog>
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
        //fuse models:
        .model fuse_coil   sw ron=1E9 roff=ohm_coil    vt=0.5
        .model fuse_switch sw ron=1E9 roff=ohm_contact vt=0.5
        IF[coil_direction]THEN
            IF[coil_direction] CONTAINS Neg && [coil_direction] CONTAINS Pos THEN //current only from pin [coil_pos] to pin [coil_neg]
                //set and hold switches(|<-------- set -------->|) || (|<---- hold --->| && |<------ not reset ----->|)
                B_set_on  coil_set 0 V=(  I(l_coil)   > ampere_on) || (V(coil_set) > 0.5 &&     I(l_coil) > ampere_off) ? 1 : 0
            ELSEIF[coil_direction]EQUAL_TO AC THEN
                //set and hold switches(|<-------- set -------->|) || (|<---- hold --->| && |<------ not reset ----->|)
                B_set_on  mid_set  0 V=(abs(I(l_coil))> ampere_on) || (V(coil_set) > 0.5 && abs(I(l_coil))> ampere_off) ? 2 : 0
                R_set_on mid_set coil_set 1 // r-c lowpass to hold for a bit more ...
                C_set_on coil_set 0 tau_n // ... than 1 tau time, to hold AC.
            ELSE
                <Dialog type="error">coil direction value "[coil_direction]" is not an allowed value</Dialog>
            
            ENDIF ENDIF
            ELSE //no [coil_direction] means, that current in any direction sets:
                //set and hold switches(|<-------- set -------->|) || (|<---- hold --->| && |<------ not reset ----->|)
                B_set_on  coil_set 0 V=(abs(I(l_coil))> ampere_on) || (V(coil_set) > 0.5 && abs(I(l_coil))> ampere_off) ? 1 : 0
        ENDIF
        //switches:
        .model model_sXa sw vt=0.5 ron=ohm_contact roff=[ohm_isolate]
        .model model_sXb sw vt=0.5 ron=[ohm_isolate] roff=ohm_contact
        s1a sw1_from sw1_midA coil_set 0 model_sXa
        s1b sw1_from sw1_midB coil_set 0 model_sXb
        IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN1THEN
        s2a sw2_from sw2_midA coil_set 0 model_sXa
        s2b sw2_from sw2_midB coil_set 0 model_sXb
        ENDIF
        .ends
        // ---- component ----
        X_relay_[individual] [coil_pos] [coil_neg] [sw1_from] IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN[sw1_toA] ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NC THEN [sw1_toB] ELSEIF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN[sw1_toA] [sw1_toB] ELSE  <Dialog type="error">types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog> ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF IF[nr_switches]HIGHER_THAN1THEN [sw2_from] IF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NO THEN [sw2_toA] ELSEIF[switch_type]EQUAL_TO NC THEN [sw2_toB]ELSEIF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO CO THEN [sw2_toA] [sw2_toB] ELSE<Dialog type="error">types of switches for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF relay_[individual]
    </Spice>
</Component>

<FINDER_41_52>
	//L Relay:FINDER-41.52
	DEFINE [datasheet] www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-41.pdf
	DEFINE [conrad_de] finder-41-52-9-012-0010-printrelais-12-v-dc-8-a-2-wechsler-1-st-503105.html
	DEFINE [nr_switches] 2
	DEFINE [switch_type] CO
	DEFINE [volt_destroy_switch] 400
	IF[modeltype]MATCHESFINDER-41\.52\.(6|8|9)\.[0-9][0-9][0-9](\.[0-9]*)?THEN
		DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:13 TO:14 OF:[modeltype]
		IF [coil_direction] EQUAL_TO 6 THEN
			<Dialog type="error">Bistable Two-coil model of Series Finder 41 is not supported. 
				Please don't use the 6 in 41.52.6.vvv but 8 for AC coil or 9 for DC coil.
				//TODO create a bistable model, must be included in default value, symbol and in spice.
			</Dialog>
		ELSE IF[coil_direction] EQUAL_TO 8 THEN 
			DEFINE [coil_direction] AC // AC model
			DEFINE [volt_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:15 TO:18 OF:[modeltype]
			IF[volt_n] EQUAL_TO 024 THEN
				DEFINE [volt_set] (19.2*1.732)//factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
				DEFINE [volt_reset] (0.45*[volt_n])
				DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] (26.4*1.732) //factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
				DEFINE [ohm_coil] 350
			ELSEIF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 230 THEN
				DEFINE [volt_set] (184*1.732)//factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
				DEFINE [volt_reset] (0.2*[volt_n])
				DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] (253*1.732)//factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
				DEFINE [ohm_coil] 32500
				
			ELSE<Dialog type="error"> [volt_n]V  is not an allowed nominal voltage for AC-type of relay model [modeltype], see [datasheet]</Dialog>
			ENDIF ENDIF
		ELSE IF[coil_direction] EQUAL_TO 9 THEN 
			DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_NULL //no direction: DC model with indifference of direction
			DEFINE [volt_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:15 TO:18 OF:[modeltype]
			
			DEFINE [volt_set] ([volt_n]*0.7)
			DEFINE [volt_reset] ([volt_n]*1.5)
			IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 110 THEN
				DEFINE [ohm_coil] 24200
			ELSE
				DEFINE [ohm_coil] ([volt_n]*[volt_n]*2.5) //5²*2.5=ca62 6²*2.5=90 12²*2.5=360 ...
			ENDIF
			
		ELSE <Dialog type="error">Unknown coil type for nr [volt_n] in model [model]</Dialog>
		ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF

	ELSE
	<Dialog type="error">
			You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series [model]
			Please select one of the available models of that series. You can do so by setting the value to:
			
			FINDER-41.52.c.nnn
			
			where:
			FINDER-40. is the model series to be written literally, (also with the dot and the bar and no spaces)
			c is the coil version in one digit: 9 for DC-coil, or 8 for AC-coil (6 for DC-bistable is not supported)
			
			nnn is the nominal voltage in three digits, one of the values:
				005 006 012 024 048 060 110 if the coil code c is 9
				024 230 if the coil code c is 8
			
			For example, FINDER-41.52.9.012 is a valid value. But the value given, [modeltype] is not.
			You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
		</Dialog>
	ENDIF
</FINDER_41_52>

<FINDER_40>
	// L Relay:FINDER-40.11
	// ALIAS Relay:FINDER-40.11-2016 Relay:FINDER-40.31 Relay:FINDER-40.41 Relay:FINDER-40.51 Relay:FINDER-40.52
	DEFINE [nr_switches] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:17 TO:18 OF:[modeltype]
	DEFINE [switch_type] CO

	IF[modeltype]MATCHESFINDER-40\.(1|3|5|6)(1|2)\.(7|8|9)\.[0-9]{3}[\.0-9]*THEN
		DEFINE [volt_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:15 TO:18 OF:[modeltype]
		DEFINE [coil_direction] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:13 TO:14 OF:[modeltype]
		IF[coil_direction]EQUAL_TO 9 THEN //standard 0.65W 
			DEFINE [coil_direction] BottomNeg_PosTop
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] ([volt_n]*1.5)
			DEFINE [volt_set] ([volt_n]*0.73)
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] (1.52*[volt_n]*[volt_n])
		ELSEIF[coil_direction]EQUAL_TO 7 THEN //sensitive 0.5W
			DEFINE [coil_direction] BottomNeg_PosTop
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] ([volt_n]*1.5)
			DEFINE [volt_set] ([volt_n]*0.73)
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] (2.0*[volt_n]*[volt_n])
		ELSEIF[coil_direction]EQUAL_TO 8 THEN
			DEFINE [coil_direction] AC // AC coil model
			DEFINE [f_n] 55 //50-60 Hertz
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] (1.1*[volt_n]*1.732) //factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
			DEFINE [volt_set] (0.8*[volt_n]*1.732) //factor 1.732=sqrt(3) because effective value, not peak
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] (0.57*[volt_n]*[volt_n])
			IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 120 THEN DEFINE [ohm_coil] 9k ENDIF
			IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 230 THEN DEFINE [ohm_coil] 28k ENDIF
			IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 240 THEN DEFINE [ohm_coil] 31500 ENDIF
		ELSE
			<Dialog type="error"> coil code [coil_direction] not defined for model [model] , component [name] , [value]</Dialog>
		ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
		DEFINE [volt_reset] ([volt_n]*0.2)    
	ELSE
		<Dialog type="error">
			You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series [model]
			Please select one of the available models of that series. You can do so by setting the value to:
			
			FINDER-40.tp.c.nnn
			
			where:
			FINDER-40. is the model series to be written literally, (also with the dot and the bar and no spaces)
			t is the pinning type in one digit, one of the values 1 3 5 6
			p is the number of poles, in one digit, 1 or 2
			c is the coil version in one digit: 7 or 9 for DC-coil, or 8 for AC-coil
			
			nnn is the nominal voltage in three digits, one of the values 005 006 007 009 012 014018 021 024 028 036 048 060 090 110 120 125 230 240
			
			For example, FINDER-40.11.9.012 is a valid value. But the value given, [value] is not.
			You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
		</Dialog>
	ENDIF
</FINDER_40>  

<FINDER_36_11>
	// L Relay:FINDER-36.11-4301
	DEFINE [datasheet] www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-36.pdf
	DEFINE [conrad_de] finder-36-11-9-012-4011-printrelais-12-v-dc-10-a-1-wechsler-1-st-503078.html
