			Please select one of the available models of that series. You can do so by setting the type to:
		
			FINDER-36.11.9.nnn
			
			where:
			FINDER-36.11.9. is the model series to be written literally, (!also with the dots!),
			nnn is the nominal voltage in three digits, one of the values 005 006 009 012 024 048 060
			
			For example, FINDER-36.11.9.012 is a valid type. But the type given, [modeltype] is not.
			You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
		</Dialog>
	ENDIF
</FINDER_36_11>

<FINDER_34_51>
	//L Relay:FINDER-34.51
	//ALIAS Relay:FINDER-34.51.7xxx.x019
	DEFINE [conrad_de] finder-34-51-7-024-0010-printrelais-24-v-dc-6-a-1-wechsler-1-st-502881.html
	DEFINE [datasheet] www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-34.pdf        
	IF[modeltype]MATCHESFINDER-34\.51\.7\.((005)|(012)|(024)|(048)|(060))(\.((0|4|5)(0|3)1(0|9))?)?THEN
		DEFINE [nr_switches] 1
		DEFINE [amp_destroy_switch] 10 //max. 6A permanent, 10A peak
		DEFINE [volt_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:15 TO:18 OF:[modeltype]
		DEFINE [switch_type] CO // also NO - type in datasheet is possible, but the models in eeschema are both CO
		//no [coil_direction]
		IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 005 THEN
			DEFINE [volt_set] 3.5 
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] 7.5
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] 130
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 012 THEN
			DEFINE [volt_set] 8.4
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] 18
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] 840
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 024 THEN
			DEFINE [volt_set] 16.8
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] 36
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] 3350
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 048 THEN
			DEFINE [volt_set] 33.6
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] 72
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] 12300
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_n] EQUAL_TO 060 THEN
			DEFINE [volt_set] 42
			DEFINE [volt_destroy_coil] 90
			DEFINE [ohm_coil] 19700
		ENDIF
		//Reset voltage is somewhere between holding voltage and drop-out voltage, see page 1 of datasheet.
		DEFINE [volt_reset] 0.2*[volt_n] 
	ELSE
		<Dialog type="error">
			You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series [model]
			Please select one of the available models of that series. You can do so by setting the type to:
		
			FINDER-34.51.7.nnn
			or 
			FINDER-34.51.7.nnn.ABCD
			
			where:
			FINDER-34.51.7. is the model series to be written literally, (!also with the dots!),
			nnn is the nominal voltage in three digits, one of the values 005 006 009 012 024 048 060
			
			A is the contact material in one digit, one of the values 0 4 5
			B is the contact circuit in one digit, one of the values 0 3 , where 0=Changeover and 3=NormallyOpen
			C is Options in one digit, only available digit for this series is 1
			D is the special versions in one digit, one of the values 0 9
			(you may omit the .ABCD block at the end, A C and D are ignored in simulation. )
			
			For example, FINDER-34.51.7.012 or FINDER-34.51.7.012.0310 are valid values. But the type given, [modeltype] is not.
			You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
		</Dialog>
	ENDIF
</FINDER_34_51>

<FINDER_32_21>
