		ENDIF
		 
</smbl_coupling>


<Component>
	<Description>
		A transformer core. Usually used together with the lcouple model above, to build a magnetic circuit
		
		---- Necessary Parameters: ----
		length, given in meters* gives the length of the way through the magnetic core.
		area, given in square meters* defines the size of the magnetic core		
				
		*(please do not write the m for meters, because the numeric interpreter will think that is milli=0,001 . Just write the number.)
		
		---- Optional parameters: ----
		calc_mode is the mode in which the core's behaviour is calculated. Must be either 1 or 2 or 7.
			modes 1 and 2 are the ngspice standard models, as defined in the user manual, chapter cm_core.
			mode 7 is a non-standard model that calculates the seven magnetic values. Mode 7 is set by default.
		
		core is the material of the magnetic core. By default it is set to esteel, which means electrical steel -which is normal to use in modern transformers.
		but you can set it to...
			... iron (standard iron, as used some decades ago)
			... sfer (soft ferrite, MnZn)
			... hfer (hard ferrite, BaFe)
			... metglas (metallic glas)  
			... mumetal (mumetal)
			... indi (individual - here you must set all parameters yourself)
		The following parameters, tau b_array h_array share_h_to_b share_m_to_b b_max h_max and permanent_h, are set by the core material, but you can overwrite them:
		
	    h_array and b_array define the shape of the B-H-curve without hysteresis, by defining a set of points in Tesla and A1/m.  
		The B-H-curve is piece-wise-linear between these points. These two arrays must have the same length. 
		
		tau is the charging time to build up a magnetic field, and affects the width of the hysteresis of the B-H-curve. The larger tau, the wider is the hysteresis.
		
		b_max and h_max are the maximal values of h_array and b_array. They are only needed for animation, not for simulation.
		
		share_h_to_b and share_m_to_b are the shares of H and M, how much they go into the combination "&" for calculating the B-field.
		Their sum should be 1, for example 0.8 and 0.2 which would mean 80% and 20%.
		The higher the share of M, the wider the hysteresis.
		
		permanent_h given in A1/m gives a permament magnet core a constant H field after a strong enough magnetisation.
		Usually set to 1.0 which is effectively nothing and permanent magnetisation is therefor off - larger values like 50 or 500 are
		advised for turning the permanent magnetisation on.
		
		There are multiple parameters called volt_per_X where X differs on each parameter.
		These parameters allow giving out the values of this core such as the H-Field or the Magnetic flow.
		By default all values are set to zero. In that case, the output is deactivated.
		Any other value than zero activates an output pin, which gives out a certain voltage V=X*volt_per_X
		These parameters are:
		volt_per_all is the general value for all seven following parameters. By setting this, you can set all seven at once:
		volt_per_mmf_ampturn gives out the magnetomotive force MMF=Θ, which has the unit ampere-turns A1.
		volt_per_h_apm gives out the H-Field which has the unit Ampereturns per Meter A1/m
		volt_per_m_apm gives out the magnetisation M, also in A1/m,
		volt_per_hm_apm gives out the combination of H & M, which is called "&" also in A1/m,
		volt_per_b_tesla gives out the B-Field which has the unit Tesla.
		volt_per_magflow gives out the magnetic flow ϕ with the unit Weber
		volt_per_magresistance gives out the resistance with the unit 1/H
		
		In calc_mode 7 any volt_per_X combination is possible. 
		In all other modes all volt_per_X are only available in this order: each volt_per_X can only be available, if the previous one is also available.
		-- additional info: --
		The simulation model not based on cm_core but complete own calculations in the spice section.
		Every step and intermediary value can be viewed by the volt_per_X parameters.
		 
	</Description>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L magnetic:core
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		area=0.01 length=0.2 // a standard core with an area of 0.01 square meters and a length of 20cm
		area=0.01 length=0.2 core=esteel // same - because esteel is the default material.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 core=iron // same - but now with the old standard cast iron.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 volt_per_b_tesla=1 animate=b // adds an output pin that gives out one volt per tesla. Also enables the magnet animation of the b-field when a wire is connected to that pin.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 volt_per_h_apm=1 animate=h // adds an output pin that gives out one volt per A1/m. Also enables the magnet animation of the h-field when a wire is connected to that pin.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 volt_per_all=1 volt_per_magresistance=1u // a core that sets enables all output voltages: most output voltages to 1V per unit, but for the magnetic resistance only 1microvolt per unit. 
		area=0.01 length=0.2 core=indi tau=1ms permanent_h=40A/m harr_phys=[-300 -200 -100 0 100 200 300] barr_phys=[-4.5 -4.5 3 0 3 4.5 4.5] h_max=300 b_max=4.5 fraction=TRUE  // an individually defined material.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 r_s_calc=1 r_p_calc=1E9 // optional resistors in the calculation path for simulation stability
		area=0.01 length=0.2 r_s_out=1 r_p_out=1E9 volt_per_all=1 // optional output resistors on the output pins for stability
		area=0.01 length=0.2 r_s_calc=1 r_p_calc=1E9 volt_per_all=1 r_s_out=1 r_p_out=1E9 // all outputs, all resistors
		area=0.01 length=0.2 calc_mode=1 // cm_core standard mode=1 : piece-wise-linear . Recommended when the default calc_mode 7 gives out error messages.
		area=0.01 length=0.2 calc_mode=2 hyst=2.3 // cm_core standard mode=2 hysteresis
		
	</Default_Values>
	<Spice>
		INCLUDE core_hmmodel_parameters 
		
		DEFINE [ohm_iso] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:Riso IN:[value] // isolation resistance between primary and secondary side
		DEFINE [ohm_iso] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm_iso]
		IF ! [ohm_iso] THEN DEFINE [ohm_iso] 1E12 ENDIF // default value

		DEFINE [area] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:area IN:[value] // area of the magnetic core
		DEFINE [area] AS_NUMBER OF:[area]
		IF ![area] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [area] 0.1 ENDIF
		DEFINE [length] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:length IN:[value] // length of the magnetic core
		DEFINE [length] AS_NUMBER OF:[length]
		IF ![length] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [length] 0.1 ENDIF
		
		DEFINE [animate] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:animate IN:[value]
		DEFINE [animate] AS_LOWERCASE OF:[animate]
		
		DEFINE [calc_mode] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:calc_mode IN:[value]
		DEFINE [calc_mode] AS_NUMBER OF:[calc_mode]
		IF ![calc_mode] THEN DEFINE [calc_mode] 7 ENDIF // 7 stands for the seven magnetic intermediate values calculated in the process below
		
		DEFINE [hyst] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:hyst IN:[value]
		DEFINE [hyst] AS_NUMBER OF:[hyst]
		
		DEFINE [fraction] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:fraction IN:[value] //fraction parameter of the h->b field calculation via pwl. See at pwl model of ngspice.
		IF ![fraction] EQUAL_TO FALSE THEN DEFINE [fraction] TRUE ENDIF
		
		// resistors in calculation block for stability
		DEFINE [r_s_calc] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_s_calc IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_p_calc] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_p_calc IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_s_out]  AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_s_out IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_p_out]  AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_p_out IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_s_calc] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_s_calc]
		DEFINE [r_p_calc] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_p_calc]
		DEFINE [r_s_out]  AS_NUMBER OF:[r_s_out] 
		DEFINE [r_p_out]  AS_NUMBER OF:[r_p_out] 
		IF ! IS_NUMBER [r_s_calc]  THEN DEFINE [r_s_calc] -1 ENDIF
		IF ! IS_NUMBER [r_p_calc]  THEN DEFINE [r_p_calc] -1 ENDIF
		IF ! IS_NUMBER [r_s_out]   THEN DEFINE [r_s_out]  -1 ENDIF
		IF ! IS_NUMBER [r_p_out]   THEN DEFINE [r_p_out]  -1 ENDIF

			
			// own calculation mode: a calculation of the magnetic values, in seven parts.
			// each part calculates a magnetic value. The last value is the magnetic resistance which controls the behaviour of this
			// magnetic core, because a core is a conductor for magnetic flow which has some resistance, just like an electric wire
			// is a conductor for electric current flow with some resistance.
			IF [calc_mode] EQUAL_TO 7 THEN 
			
			// subcircuit defining the magnetic core
			.subckt core_b_[individual] pin1 pin2 IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN mmf ENDIF IF[volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN hfield ENDIF IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magnetisation ENDIF IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN h_and_m ENDIF IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN bfield ENDIF IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magflow ENDIF IF[volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magresistance ENDIF //   
		
				// Part 1: calculate the magnetomotive force "MMF": 
				B_MMF   mmf_calc 0 V=V(pin1)-V(pin2)
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_s mmf_calc mmf_loc [r_s_calc] // serial resistor for simulation stability
				ELSE V_MMF_S mmf_calc mmf_loc DC 0 ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_p mmf_calc 0       [r_p_calc] ENDIF  // parallel resistor for simulation stability
				
				IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_MMF_out   mmf_out 0 V=V(mmf_loc)*[volt_per_mmf_ampturn] // output of mmf (Ampereturn -> Volt)
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_out_s mmf_out mmf [r_s_out]
					ELSE                            V_MMF_out_s mmf_out mmf DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_out_p mmf_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				
				// Part 2: calculate the H-Field value 
				B_H hfield_loc 0 V=V(mmf_loc)/[length]
				IF [volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
					B_H_out   hfield_out 0 V=V(hfield_loc)*[volt_per_h_apm] // output of hfield ( Ampereturn/Meter=A1/m -> Volt)
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_H_out_s hfield_out hfield [r_s_out] 
					ELSE                            V_H_out_s hfield_out hfield DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_H_out_p hfield_out 0    [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
			
				// Part 3: magnetisation, by rc lowpass simulating the magnetisation time, and two zener diodes simulating remanence
				// 3a: diodes for remanence (keeping up a certain degree of magnetisation/ magnetic polarisation within the core material) 
				IF [permanent_h] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					.model mdl_zener_diode D BV=[permanent_h] 
					Dmag1 hfield_loc node_magD1 mdl_zener_diode
					Dmag2 node_magD2 node_magD1 mdl_zener_diode
				ELSE
					V_dmag hfield_loc node_magD2 DC 0 // connection instead of the diodes
				ENDIF
				// 3b: rc lowpass defines the characteristic time "tau" in which the core material gets magnetised
				Rmag_s node_magD2 magnetisation_loc 1 
				Cmag  magnetisation_loc 0 [tau] 
				
				IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
					B_M_out   magnetisation_out 0 V=V(magnetisation_loc)*[volt_per_m_apm]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_M_out_s magnetisation_out magnetisation [r_s_out]
					ELSE                            V_M_out_s magnetisation_out magnetisation DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_M_out_p magnetisation_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				// 3c: parallel resistance only for simulation stability. (very high resistance therefor very low distortion)
				Rmag_p node_magD2 0 1E12 
				
				// Part 4: combine H-Field and magnetisation to a combined value called h_and_m
				B_HnM h_and_m_calc 0 V=[share_h_to_b]*V(hfield_loc)+[share_m_to_b]*V(magnetisation_loc)
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_s h_and_m_calc h_and_m_loc [r_s_calc] 
				ELSE                             V_HnM_s h_and_m_calc h_and_m_loc DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_p h_and_m_calc 0           [r_p_calc] ENDIF
				IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_HnM_out   h_and_m_out 0 V=V(h_and_m_loc)*[volt_per_hm_apm]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_out_s h_and_m_out h_and_m [r_s_out]
					ELSE                            V_HnM_out_s h_and_m_out h_and_m DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_out_p h_and_m_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				
				// Part 5: calculate the B-field based on the h_and_m
				.model pwl_bfield pwl(x_array=[harr_phys] y_array=[barr_phys] fraction=[fraction])
				a_bfield h_and_m_loc bfield_calc pwl_bfield
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rs_bfield bfield_calc bfield_loc [r_s_calc] // series resistor for stability 
				ELSE Vs_bfield bfield_calc bfield_loc DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_bfield bfield_loc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF // parallel resistor for stability
				
				IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
					B_B_out   bfield_out 0 V=V(bfield_loc)*[volt_per_b_tesla]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_B_out_s bfield_out bfield [r_s_out] 
					ELSE V_B_out bfield_out bfield DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_B_out_p bfield_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				// Part 6: make a magnetic flow current 
				B_phi magflow_calc 0 V=V(bfield_loc)*[area]
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_phi magflow_calc magflow_loc [r_s_calc] 
				ELSE                             V_phi magflow_calc magflow_loc DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_phi magflow_calc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
				
				IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
					B_magflow_out   magflow_out 0 V=V(magflow_loc)*[volt_per_magflow]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magflow_out_s magflow_out magflow [r_s_out] 
					ELSE V_magflow_out magflow_out magflow DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magflow_out_p magflow_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				
				// Part 7: make a resistance so that this flow current is at the mmf
				// 7a - preparation of division variable, to be not zero.
				B_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc 0 V=V(magflow_calc)<-1E-12?V(magflow_calc):V(magflow_calc)>1E-12?V(magflow_calc):1E-12
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc magflow_nozero [r_s_calc]
				ELSE							 V_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc magflow_nozero DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_phi_nozero magflow_nozero 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
				
				// 7b - calculate magnetic resistance
				B_res magresistance_calc 0 V=V(mmf_loc)/V(magflow_nozero)
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_res_s magresistance_calc magresistance_loc [r_s_calc]  // series resistor for stability
				ELSE                             V_res_s magresistance_calc magresistance_loc DC 0
				ENDIF 
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_res_p magresistance_calc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
				IF [volt_per_magresistance]LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_magresistance_out magresistance_out 0 V=V(magresistance_loc)*[volt_per_magresistance];
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magresistance_s   magresistance_out magresistance [r_s_out] 
					ELSE V_magresistance_out magresistance_out magresistance 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magresistance_p   magresistance_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				ENDIF
				// final part : give out the magnetic flow value 
				R_core pin1 pin2 r=V(magresistance_loc);
				
			.ends
			// Instantiate the transformer subcircuit:
			X_core_[individual] [pin1] [pin2] IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [mmf] ENDIFIF[volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [hfield] ENDIF IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magnetisation] ENDIF  IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [h_and_m] ENDIF IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [bfield] ENDIF IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magflow] ENDIF IF [volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magresistance] ENDIF core_b_[individual]

			
			ELSE // all calc_mode values other than 7:
				// subcircuit defining the magnetic core
				.subckt core_b_[individual] pin1 pin2 IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN mmf  IF[volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN hfield  IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magnetisation  IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN h_and_m  IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN bfield  IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magflow  IF[volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN magresistance  //   
				ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
				
			ENDIF //END OF calc mode seven_mag
			// ngspice standard core PWL calculation as defined in the ngspice user manual, section "cm_core" with  
			// PWL Mode (mode=1)
			IF [calc_mode] EQUAL_TO 1 THEN  
					.model pwl_core_[individual] core (mode=1 area=[area] length=[length] H_array=[harr_phys] B_array=[barr_phys])					
					a_core (pin1 pin2) pwl_core_[individual]  
			ENDIF
			// ngspice standard core PWL calculation as defined in the ngspice user manual, section "cm_core" with  
			// HYSTERESIS Mode (mode=2)
			IF [calc_mode] EQUAL_TO 2 THEN					
					IF [hyst] IS_NUMBER && [hyst] HIGHER_THAN 0 && [b_max] HIGHER_THAN 0 && [h_max] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN							
						.model hyst_core_[individual] core (mode=2 area=[area] length=[length]
						+ in_low=-[h_max] in_high=[h_max]
						+ out_lower_limit=-[b_max] out_upper_limit=[b_max]
						+ hyst = [hyst])
						a_core (pin1 pin2) hyst_core_[individual] 
					ELSE
						<Dialog type="error" title= "core hysteresis mode needs hyst b_max and h_max parameters">
							Error: a magnetic hysteresis needs the boundaries for b and h values and the hyst parameter,
							and they must be positive, larger than zero.
							But at least one of these is not given or not positive:
							hyst=[hyst]   , the width of the hysteresis)
							h_max=[h_max] , defining the input boundaries in_low and in_high as -1 and +1 x h_max  
							b_max=[b_max] , defining the output boundaries out_lower_limit and out_upper_limit as -1 and +1 x b_max
							Please check the hysteresis mode of the cm_core model in the ngspice user manual.
						</Dialog>
					ENDIF
			ENDIF	
			// give out the  seven magnetic as used above for calc_mode 7 for all other modes:
			IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 THEN
				// Part 1: calculate the magnetomotive force "MMF":
				IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_MMF   mmf_calc 0 V=V(pin1)-V(pin2)
					IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_s mmf_calc mmf_loc [r_s_calc] // serial resistor for simulation stability
					ELSE V_MMF_S mmf_calc mmf_loc DC 0 ENDIF
					IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_p mmf_calc 0       [r_p_calc] ENDIF  // parallel resistor for simulation stability

					// IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
						B_MMF_out   mmf_out 0 V=V(mmf_loc)*[volt_per_mmf_ampturn] // output of mmf (Ampereturn -> Volt)
						IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_out_s mmf_out mmf [r_s_out]
						ELSE                            V_MMF_out_s mmf_out mmf DC 0
						ENDIF
						IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_MMF_out_p mmf_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
					// ENDIF
					
				// Part 2: calculate the H-Field value 
				IF[volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_H hfield_loc 0 V=V(mmf_loc)/[length]
					
					//IF [volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
						B_H_out   hfield_out 0 V=V(hfield_loc)*[volt_per_h_apm] // output of hfield ( Ampereturn/Meter=A1/m -> Volt)
						IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_H_out_s hfield_out hfield [r_s_out] 
						ELSE                            V_H_out_s hfield_out hfield DC 0
						ENDIF
						IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_H_out_p hfield_out 0    [r_p_out] ENDIF
					//ENDIF
				// Part 3: magnetisation, by rc lowpass simulating the magnetisation time, and two zener diodes simulating remanence
				IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
				// 3a: diodes for remanence (keeping up a certain degree of magnetisation/ magnetic polarisation within the core material) 
					IF [permanent_h] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
						.model mdl_zener_diode D BV=[permanent_h] 
						Dmag1 hfield_loc node_magD1 mdl_zener_diode
						Dmag2 node_magD2 node_magD1 mdl_zener_diode
					ELSE
						V_dmag hfield_loc node_magD2 DC 0 // connection instead of the diodes
					ENDIF
				
				// 3b: rc lowpass defines the characteristic time "tau" in which the core material gets magnetised
					Rmag_s node_magD2 magnetisation_loc 1 
					Cmag  magnetisation_loc 0 [tau] 
					
					//IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
						B_M_out   magnetisation_out 0 V=V(magnetisation_loc)*[volt_per_m_apm]
						IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_M_out_s magnetisation_out magnetisation [r_s_out]
						ELSE                            V_M_out_s magnetisation_out magnetisation DC 0
						ENDIF
						IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_M_out_p magnetisation_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
					//ENDIF
				// 3c: parallel resistance only for simulation stability. (very high resistance therefor very low distortion)
					Rmag_p node_magD2 0 1E12 

				
				// Part 4: combine H-Field and magnetisation to a combined value called h_and_m
				IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN

				B_HnM h_and_m_calc 0 V=[share_h_to_b]*V(hfield_loc)+[share_m_to_b]*V(magnetisation_loc)
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_s h_and_m_calc h_and_m_loc [r_s_calc] 
				ELSE                             V_HnM_s h_and_m_calc h_and_m_loc DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_p h_and_m_calc 0           [r_p_calc] ENDIF

				//IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_HnM_out   h_and_m_out 0 V=V(h_and_m_loc)*[volt_per_hm_apm]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_out_s h_and_m_out h_and_m [r_s_out]
					ELSE                            V_HnM_out_s h_and_m_out h_and_m DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_HnM_out_p h_and_m_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				//ENDIF
				
				// Part 5: calculate the B-field based on the h_and_m
				IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
				
				.model pwl_bfield pwl(x_array=[harr_phys] y_array=[barr_phys] fraction=[fraction])
				a_bfield h_and_m_loc bfield_calc pwl_bfield
				IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rs_bfield bfield_calc bfield_loc [r_s_calc] // series resistor for stability 
				ELSE Vs_bfield bfield_calc bfield_loc DC 0
				ENDIF
				IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_bfield bfield_loc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF // parallel resistor for stability
				
				//IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
					B_B_out   bfield_out 0 V=V(bfield_loc)*[volt_per_b_tesla]
					IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_B_out_s bfield_out bfield [r_s_out] 
					ELSE V_B_out bfield_out bfield DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_B_out_p bfield_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
				//ENDIF
				
				// Part 6: make a magnetic flow current 
				IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					B_phi magflow_calc 0 V=V(bfield_loc)*[area]
					IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_phi magflow_calc magflow_loc [r_s_calc] 
					ELSE                             V_phi magflow_calc magflow_loc DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_phi magflow_calc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
					
					//IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN 
						B_magflow_out   magflow_out 0 V=V(magflow_loc)*[volt_per_magflow]
						IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magflow_out_s magflow_out magflow [r_s_out] 
						ELSE V_magflow_out magflow_out magflow DC 0
						ENDIF
						IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magflow_out_p magflow_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
					//ENDIF
					
				// Part 7: make a resistance so that this flow current is at the mmf
				IF [volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
				
					// 7a - preparation of division variable, to be not zero.
					B_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc 0 V=V(magflow_calc)<-1E-12?V(magflow_calc):V(magflow_calc)>1E-12?V(magflow_calc):1E-12
					IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc magflow_nozero [r_s_calc]
					ELSE							 V_phi_nozero magflow_nozero_loc magflow_nozero DC 0
					ENDIF
					IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN rp_phi_nozero magflow_nozero 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
					
					// 7b - calculate magnetic resistance
					B_res magresistance_calc 0 V=V(mmf_loc)/V(magflow_nozero)
					IF [r_s_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_res_s magresistance_calc magresistance_loc [r_s_calc]  // series resistor for stability
					ELSE                             V_res_s magresistance_calc magresistance_loc DC 0
					ENDIF 
					IF [r_p_calc] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_res_p magresistance_calc 0 [r_p_calc] ENDIF
					//IF [volt_per_magresistance]LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
						B_magresistance_out magresistance_out 0 V=V(magresistance_loc)*[volt_per_magresistance];
						IF [r_s_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magresistance_s   magresistance_out magresistance [r_s_out] 
						ELSE V_magresistance_out magresistance_out magresistance 0
						ENDIF
						IF [r_p_out] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN R_magresistance_p   magresistance_out 0 [r_p_out] ENDIF
					//ENDIF
				ENDIF // Part 7 end.
				ENDIF // Part 6 end.
				ENDIF // Part 5 end.
				ENDIF // Part 4 end.
				ENDIF // Part 3 end.
				ENDIF // Part 2 end.
				ENDIF // Part 1 end.
				.ends
				// Instantiate the transformer subcircuit:
				X_core_[individual] [pin1] [pin2] IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [mmf] IF[volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [hfield]  IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magnetisation] IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [h_and_m]  IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [bfield]  IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magflow]  IF [volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN [magresistance] ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF core_b_[individual]
			ENDIF
		
	</Spice>
	<animation>
		IF [animate] EQUAL_TO b THEN
			DEFINE [b_act] V[bfield] // b field equivalent in volt
			IF [b_act] IS_NUMBER THEN 
				// calculate share of actual b-field vs maximal b-field
				DEFINE [b_act] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[b_act] AND:[volt_per_b_tesla] // actual value of b field in tesla
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[b_act] AND:[b_max] // animation x-coordinate:
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:350 // positive coordinate
				DEFINE [mag_neg] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:-1 // negative coordinate
				//
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_pos] 100 #800000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% red rectangle for one magnetic pole
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_neg] 100 #008000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% green rectangle for other magnetic pole
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		IF [animate] EQUAL_TO m THEN
			DEFINE [m_act] V[magnetisation] // magnetisation equivalent in volt
			IF [m_act] IS_NUMBER THEN 
				DEFINE [m_act] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[m_act] AND:[volt_per_m_apm] // magnetisation in A/m
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[m_act] AND:[h_max] // animation x-coordinate:
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:350 // positive coordinate
				DEFINE [mag_neg] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:-1 // negative coordinate
				//
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_pos] 100 #800000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% red rectangle for one magnetic pole
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_neg] 100 #008000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% green rectangle for other magnetic pole
			ENDIF
		ENDIF	
		IF [animate] EQUAL_TO h THEN
			DEFINE [h_act] V[hfield] // h field equivalent in volt
			IF [h_act] IS_NUMBER THEN
				DEFINE [h_act] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[h_act] AND:[volt_per_h_apm] // actual value of h field in A/m
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[h_act] AND:[h_max] // animation x-coordinate:
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:350 // positive coordinate
				DEFINE [mag_neg] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:-1 // negative coordinate
				//
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_pos] 100 #800000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% red rectangle for one magnetic pole
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_neg] 100 #008000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% green rectangle for other magnetic pole
			ENDIF			
		ENDIF
		IF [animate] CONTAINS & THEN // combination of h and m
			DEFINE [hm_act] V[h_and_m] // combination of h field and magnetisation,  equivalent in volt
			IF [hm_act] IS_NUMBER THEN
				DEFINE [hm_act] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[h_act] AND:[volt_per_hm_apm] // actual value of h&m field in A/m
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[hm_act] AND:[h_max] // animation x-coordinate:
				DEFINE [mag_pos] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:350 // positive coordinate
				DEFINE [mag_neg] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[mag_pos] AND:-1 // negative coordinate
				//
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_pos] 100 #800000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% red rectangle for one magnetic pole
				<Rectangle 0 -250 [mag_neg] 100 #008000 2 1 #000080 2 0.6> //60% green rectangle for other magnetic pole
			ENDIF
		
		ENDIF
	</animation>
	<eeschema_symbol>
		DEFINE [volt_per_all] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_all IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_all] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_all]
		IF ![volt_per_all] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_all] 0 ENDIF
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_mmf_ampturn IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_mmf_ampturn]  IN:[value]
		IF    ![volt_per_mmf_ampturn] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_h_apm] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_h_apm IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_h_apm] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_h_apm]  IN:[value]
		IF    ![volt_per_h_apm] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_h_apm] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_h_apm] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_m_apm] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_m_apm IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_m_apm] AS_NUMBER OF: [volt_per_m_apm]  IN:[value]
		IF    ![volt_per_m_apm] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_m_apm] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_h_apm] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_m_apm] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_hm_apm] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_hm_apm IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_hm_apm] AS_NUMBER OF: [volt_per_hm_apm]  IN:[value]
		IF    ![volt_per_hm_apm] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_hm_apm] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_m_apm] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_hm_apm] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.
	  
		DEFINE [volt_per_b_tesla] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_b_tesla IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_b_tesla] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_b_tesla]  IN:[value]
		IF    ![volt_per_b_tesla] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_b_tesla] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_hm_apm] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_b_tesla] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_magflow] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_magflow IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_magflow] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_magflow]  IN:[value]
		IF ![volt_per_magflow] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_magflow] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_b_tesla] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_magflow] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.
		
		DEFINE [volt_per_magresistance] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt_per_magresistance IN:[value]
		DEFINE [volt_per_magresistance] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt_per_magresistance]  IN:[value]
		IF ![volt_per_magresistance] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [volt_per_magresistance] [volt_per_all] ENDIF
		IF [calc_mode] LOWER_THAN 7 && [volt_per_magflow] EQUAL_TO 0 THEN DEFINE [volt_per_magresistance] 0 ENDIF // in modes 1 and 2 all values depend on its previous one.

		// pins:
		(pin bidirectional line (at -7.62 -1.27 90) (length 2.54)
		  (name "pin1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
		(pin bidirectional line (at 7.62 -1.27 90) (length 2.54)
		  (name "pin2" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "2" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
		// optional pins
		IF [volt_per_mmf_ampturn] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at -7.62 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "mmf" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "3" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			// MMF is short for "magnetomotive force" (theta Θ character would be okay here too)
			(text "MMF" (at -9.5 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_per_h_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at -5.08 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "hfield" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "4" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			(text "H" (at -5.68 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_per_m_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at -2.54 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "magnetisation" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "5" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			(text "M" (at -3.1 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF		
		IF [volt_per_hm_apm] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at 0 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "h_and_m" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "6" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			(text "&" (at -0.64 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_per_b_tesla] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at 2.54 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "bfield" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "7" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			(text "B" (at 2.0 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		
		IF [volt_per_magflow] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at 5.08 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "magflow" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "8" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			// Phi symbol "ϕ" is not standard ASCII character
			
			// combining Phi symbol out ASCII characters O and I = ϕ
			(text "o" (at 4.5 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
			(text "|" (at 4.5 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		IF [volt_per_magresistance] LOWER_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
			(pin bidirectional line (at 7.62 8.89 270) (length 2.0)
			  (name "magresistance" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			  (number "8" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
			)
			(text "R" (at 7.0 7.2 0)
				(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)))
			)
		ENDIF
		// core symbol:
		(polyline
			  (pts
				(xy -6.35 1.27)
				(xy -6.35 3.81)
				(xy 6.35 3.81)
				(xy 6.35 1.27)
				(xy 8.89 1.27)
				(xy 8.89 6.35)
				(xy -8.89 6.35)
				(xy -8.89 1.27)
				(xy -6.35 1.27)
			  )
			  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
			  (fill (type background))
			)
		)
		// 3d lines of the core:
		(polyline
		  (pts
			(xy -8.89 6.35)
			(xy -7.62 7.62)
			(xy 10.16 7.62)
		  )
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)
		(polyline
		  (pts
			(xy 8.89 1.27)
			(xy 10.16 2.54)
			(xy 10.16 7.62)
			(xy 8.89 6.35)
		  )
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)	
	</eeschema_symbol>
</Component>

<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN 
			Ein Luftspalt im Eisenkern. 
			Definiert durch die räumliche dreidimensionale Grösse, vereinfacht als Rechteck. 
			
			Kann verwendet werden, um offene Kerne zu simulieren:
			Es berechnet den magnetischen Widerstand eines solchen Luftspaltes als Rm=length / (u0 * ur *area)
			
			
		ELSE
			An air gap in the iron core.
			Defined by the three dimensional size, simplified as a rectangle.
			
			Can be used to simulate open cores.
			It calculates the magnetic resistance of such an air gap as Rm=length/ (u0 * ur * area)
		ENDIF
	</Description>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L magnetic:air_gap
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		length=0.1 area=0.02 // an air gap with 0.1m=100mm length and an area of 0.02 square meters.
		length=0.1 area=0.02 u_r=1.0000004 // air gap with given permeability value u_r
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_symbol>

		(rectangle (start -3.81 2.54) (end 1.27 -3.81)
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)
		(polyline
		  (pts
			(xy 1.27 2.54)
			(xy 3.81 5.08)
		  )
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)
		(polyline
		  (pts
			(xy -3.81 2.54)
			(xy -1.27 5.08)
			(xy 3.81 5.08)
			(xy 3.81 -1.27)
			(xy 1.27 -3.81)
		  )
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)
		(pin input line (at 0 6.35 270) (length 2.54)
		  (name "pin1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
		(pin input line (at 0 -5.08 90) (length 1.27)
		  (name "pin2" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "2" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
	</eeschema_symbol>
	
	<Spice>
		DEFINE [length] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:length IN:[value]
		DEFINE [length] AS_NUMBER OF:[length]
		
		DEFINE [area] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:area IN:[value]
		DEFINE [area] AS_NUMBER OF:[area]
		
		// the magnetic constant u_0 and the material constant u_r 
		DEFINE [u_r] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:u_r IN:[value]
		DEFINE [u_r] AS_NUMBER OF:[u_r]
		IF ![u_r] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [u_r] 1.0 ENDIF // u_r is 1.0 by default. That is the value for vacuum, but air is not much different.
		
		//
		IF [length] IS_NUMBER && [area] IS_NUMBER THENELSE
			<Dialog type="error" title="missing parameter for air gap">
				The air gap in the magnetic core is not defined correctly, it needs the length and area.
				Please check whether these parameters have correct values given and that they are written correctly.
			</Dialog>
		ENDIF
		
		// nominal B field value for animation.
		DEFINE [b_nom] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:b_nom IN:[value]
		DEFINE [b_nom] AS_NUMBER OF:[b_nom]
		IF ![b_nom] IS_NUMBER THEN DEFINE [b_nom] 0.2 ENDIF 
		
		// equivalent ohms, since this air gap is designed to be used in a magnetic equivalent circuit, where magnetic Resistance and 
	    // each electric Resistance can be replaced by each other, so that electric Ohm equals magnetic 1/H: 
		DEFINE [u0ur] AS_MATH_MUL OF:1.256637061E-6 AND:[u_r]
		DEFINE [eq_ohms] AS_CALCULATION OF: [length]/([u0ur] * [area]) // equivalent ohms where ohm=1/H 
		R_equivalent [pin1] [pin2] [eq_ohms] 
	</Spice>
	<animation>
		DEFINE [act_mflow] I[pin1]
		IF [act_mflow] IS_NUMBER && [area] IS_NUMBER THEN
			DEFINE [act_bfield] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[act_mflow] AND:[area]
			
			DEFINE [opacity] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[act_bfield] AND:[b_nom]
			IF [opacity] LOWER_THAN 0 THEN 
				DEFINE [] AS_MATH_SUB OF:0 AND:[opacity]
			ENDIF
			IF [opacity] LOWER_THAN 0.1 THEN 
				DEFINE [opacity] 0.1 
			ENDIF
			IF [opacity] HIGHER_THAN 1 THEN 
				DEFINE [opacity] 1.0 
			ENDIF
			DEFINE [arrlen] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[opacity] AND:200
			
			IF [act_mflow] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN // arrow pointing down
				// <Rectangle -100 -100 30 220 #000080 2 1 #000080 2 [opacity]>	
				<Line -100 0  30 -30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -100 0 -30 -30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -100 0 0 -[arrlen] #000080 2 1>
				
				<Line -20 0  30 -30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -20 0 -30 -30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -20 0 0 -[arrlen] #000080 2 1>
				
				<Text -60 10 70 #000080 90 "B">
			ENDIF
		
			IF [act_mflow] LOWER_THAN 0 THEN // arrow pointing up
				// <Rectangle -100 -80 30 220 #000080 2 1 #000080 2 [opacity]>
				<Line -100 0  30 30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -100 0 -30 30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -100 0 0 [arrlen] #000080 2 1>
				
				<Line -20 0  30 30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -20 0 -30 30       #000080 2 1>
				<Line -20 0 0 [arrlen] #000080 2 1>
				
				<Text -60 -30 70 #000080 90 "B">
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
	</animation>
</Component>

// ---- End of Part 2a - Transformer parts ----
	
